More interactive USD edits of a point instancer, with the usd procedural cache_id and with the render delegate

A point instancer of a cube has its prototype size and its instance scales edited, and its scales removed. A sphere
prototype is added to its prototypes and the cube one removed, it's hidden and shown again, it's excluded from and
included again in the light link collection of the light, and gets a per-instance displayColor primvar, edited and
removed. The stage is re-rendered after each edit.
The scenario runs with the "usd" procedural (hydra reader) reading the stage through its cache_id in an interactive
render session, and with the HdArnoldRendererPlugin render delegate driven like a Hydra host, see
testsuite/common/interactive_usd_test.h. Each render is checked in test.cpp, and the procedural render of step 9 is
compared against the reference image. Edits that aren't rendered correctly yet are reported as warnings (known issues
in test.cpp).

author: sebastien.blaineau.ortega@autodesk.com

PARAMS: {'program_env': 'interactive_usd'}
